add('# Classic opportunity projection repair')
add('\nResearch only. Default remains `legacy_v1`; **do not promote `team_window_v2` yet**. No server restart, active projection update, optimizer scoring change or database mutation was performed. Original Week 5 snapshots and the root-cause audit are unchanged.')
add('\nThe general allocation defect is confirmed and repaired behind an explicit opt-in policy. Frozen Week 5 results support 17.00 carries for Gibbs and 8.00 targets for Wilson. Available historical validation does **not** establish that the complete corrected projection pipeline is better. The restricted-source Week 4 comparison has worse MAE and opportunity errors despite a small RMSE improvement, but cannot isolate allocation quality because its original raw-input parity fails.')
add('\n## Root cause and implementation')
add('\n`canonical_projection_inputs.attach_lagged_opportunity_features` previously used each player’s last three appearances, including previous-team and stale workloads. `apply_pregame_projection_context` divided these incompatible shares by their pooled sum when above 1.0, then removed unavailable players’ assignments. Unavailable old-team history could also activate a team-wide opportunity anchor. `predictions.apply_opportunity_point_adjustment` then blended the distorted workload anchor into the historical/model mean at 55%. These are upstream projection paths; optimizer exclusions did not cause the defect.')
add('\nThe repair changes only `canonical_projection_inputs.py`, `predictions.py`, the new `opportunity_history.py` and the default-off configuration in `config.py`. It uses canonical IDs, current salary-team membership after the target-team override, normalized team abbreviations and one common last-three-team-game window strictly before the target period. Source revisions received after the cutoff are excluded before canonical deduplication. FB statistics join the RB denominator, matching DraftKings positions. Historical WR/QB carries cannot be translated into the RB pool.')
add('\nShares are aggregate same-team player counts divided by aggregate team counts over that common window. A player absent from a known team game contributes no observed workload for that game. No same-team rows at all remains missing evidence; its public projected count is unknown, not a confident zero. Explicit sourced current counts/shares can support new roles. Same-team observations after a trade are averaged over the shared window, without importing the former team’s role. Prior-season fallback remains possible when recent-season observations were not available; this is an important remaining freshness limitation.')
add('\nMeasured shares are not inflated to exhaust the eligible salary pool. Availability removes genuine same-team workload; stale or other-team history has zero vacated share. Explicit counts override supported player estimates; other estimates may be reduced to respect team capacity. Redistribution retains existing evidence/assumption requirements and is capped by both genuine vacated work and remaining capacity. No player-specific rules were added. Every team/opportunity audit includes historical shares, unrepresented volume, removed share, requested/actual redistribution, recipient support, allocated and unallocated volume.')
add('\nAnchors activate for explicit current opportunity evidence or genuinely removed same-team work, and only for players with relevant measured or explicit workload evidence. A former-team ghost alone no longer activates them. The veteran 55% and low-history 70% coefficients, fitted isotonic anchors, model weights and residual calibration profiles are unchanged. No coefficient tuning was attempted.')
add('\nConfiguration: `PLAYER_OPPORTUNITY_ALLOCATION_POLICY=legacy_v1` is the default. `team_window_v2` is reserved for research. Production `load_inputs` records policy/window lineage; direct `prepare_inputs` callers retain their existing default unless explicitly opted in. Future opt-in training would rebuild opportunity-derived features; this experiment deliberately keeps fitted training data, weights and profiles fixed.')
add('\n## Frozen replay and Gibbs/Wilson calculations')
